{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393615-elders-in-changeling-the-dreaming","id":1393615,"title":"\"Elders\" in Changeling the Dreaming","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-06-02T06:25:10-07:00","id":1393615,"title":"\"Elders\" in Changeling the Dreaming","content":"This is my first post here. As the information doesn't come in the book, or at least I didn't see it. I would like to know how the &quot;elders&quot; in Changeling are, the characters that would be comparable to the famous &quot;Methuselahs&quot; of &quot;Vampire the Masquerade&quot;, since in Changeling there is no characteristic that compares the level of power like the &quot;Generation&quot;. I decided to ask because in the book there is no information for the creation of &quot;more powerful&quot; characters. <br /> What determines that a character has reached this level of power? Or such characters are not possible in Changeling the Dreaming?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25762-yuesidhe","name":"YueSidhe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T07:31:36-07:00","id":1393625,"title":"","content":"If we're talking about Methuselah-level, the closest are the Fomorians and Tuatha de Danaan, who are basically a different order of being from changelings (and have never been statted).<br /> <br /> That said, there is a potential 'next stage' for changelings: becoming one of the immortal Siochi\u00e1n. They're not powerhouses like Methuselahs are, but they do get their own set of advantages: they never age and will never die from natural causes, gain an additional dot of Glamour and Willpower upon their ascension, and can resist both Bedlam and Banality. However, becoming Siochi\u00e1n means committing themselves to upholding a Mantle, an iconic archetype like the Boogeyman and the Knight-Errant. Details are given in the C20 Player's Guide.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T08:05:13-07:00","id":1393637,"title":"","content":"True Fae wouldn\u2019t be limited by Mortal form, so far only the Fomorians have awakened like the a Lady With Bones for Hands.<br /> <br /> But Fae Magic like Arts have Unleashings, and they are like if pretty much all Fae had Access to limited use of Archmagic. Fae Can truly come off as Gods.<br /> <br /> You also have Fae that can live centuries by extending their life through Freeholds.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T09:50:27-07:00","id":1393660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393615-elders-in-changeling-the-dreaming?p=1393625#post1393625\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If we're talking about Methuselah-level, the closest are the Fomorians and Tuatha de Danaan, who are basically a different order of being from changelings (and have never been statted).<br /> <br /> That said, there is a potential 'next stage' for changelings: becoming one of the immortal Siochi\u00e1n. They're not powerhouses like Methuselahs are, but they do get their own set of advantages: they never age and will never die from natural causes, gain an additional dot of Glamour and Willpower upon their ascension, and can resist both Bedlam and Banality. However, becoming Siochi\u00e1n means committing themselves to upholding a Mantle, an iconic archetype like the Boogeyman and the Knight-Errant. Details are given in the C20 Player's Guide.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I imagined that Siochi\u00e1n were the &quot;equivalent&quot; to &quot;Golkonda&quot; for vampires. Sorry to be comparing, is that I know more about vampire, than changeling. Although my favorite lineage is Kiasyd.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25762-yuesidhe","name":"YueSidhe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T10:42:39-07:00","id":1393672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>YueSidhe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393615-elders-in-changeling-the-dreaming?p=1393660#post1393660\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagined that Siochi\u00e1n were the &quot;equivalent&quot; to &quot;Golkonda&quot; for vampires. Sorry to be comparing, is that I know more about vampire, than changeling. Although my favorite lineage is Kiasyd.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda-sorta? Both are spiritual journeys, but where Golconda is inward-focused, looking for personal enlightenment (whatever form that takes for Kindred), becoming Siochi\u00e1n is outward-focused, taking up a responsibility to the Dreaming (and can be willingly set down again).<br /> <br /> (Also, while Golconda's existence and nature is up for grabs, becoming Siochi\u00e1n is real, if shrouded in legend, and there're enough of them for Siochi\u00e1n of given regions to arrange social meetings.)<br /> <br /> Changelings have nothing like diablerie, nothing that could potentially put them on a whole new power level; the quest for that kind of power has never been part of the game's themes, unlike Vampire and Mage. Becoming Siochi\u00e1n is the closest they get.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T12:16:46-07:00","id":1393683,"title":"","content":"Are there 6+ powers? no. Are there powers that easily rival Elder discplines? absolutely. Scene alone gives changelings elder discpline qualities. I can say set everyone in an apratment on fire.. turn into a dragon, raise the dead....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T13:40:15-07:00","id":1393695,"title":"","content":"I Belive a changeling with multiple 5 dot arts and complete mastery over realms will be on equal footing with a mathuselah if you also consider that a changeling of such powers will have powerful chimera companions (like dragons) and unique treasures (like a mirror that allows you to cast arts into a target at the other side of the world)<br /> <br /> <br /> While such changeling might not have arts over 5 dots, he beats any mathuselah in sheer versatility. People often sleep on how powerful having all realms really is. <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26021-rucun","name":"Rucun","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T15:43:44-07:00","id":1393706,"title":"","content":"There are no 6+ dot powers, and Changelings who try to live for hundreds of years almost always fall to Bedlam by then.<br /> <br /> There are big scary old things in the game of Changeling the Dreaming, but they're not &quot;player characters but older&quot; like in Vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10243-zenten","name":"zenten","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10243_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"488"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T17:41:43-07:00","id":1393717,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393615-elders-in-changeling-the-dreaming?p=1393637#post1393637\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">True Fae wouldn\u2019t be limited by Mortal form, so far only the Fomorians have awakened like the a Lady With Bones for Hands.<br /> <br /> But Fae Magic like Arts have Unleashings, and they are like if pretty much all Fae had Access to limited use of Archmagic. Fae Can truly come off as Gods.<br /> <br /> You also have Fae that can live centuries by extending their life through Freeholds.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Where is the Lady With Bones for Hands mentioned? And other Fomori awakening?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/412-valismedsen","name":"valismedsen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar412_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"391"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T18:34:00-07:00","id":1393721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>valismedsen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393615-elders-in-changeling-the-dreaming?p=1393717#post1393717\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Where is the Lady With Bones for Hands mentioned? And other Fomori awakening?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it was Dreams and Nightmares. I think she was surprisingly resistant to banality, and if the line continued they would have introduced more of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T18:57:41-07:00","id":1393724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenten</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393615-elders-in-changeling-the-dreaming?p=1393706#post1393706\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are no 6+ dot powers, and Changelings who try to live for hundreds of years almost always fall to Bedlam by then.<br /> <br /> There are big scary old things in the game of Changeling the Dreaming, but they're not &quot;player characters but older&quot; like in Vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Siochain, anyone with a 1 point merit, even without it 200 years is probably not super impossible for a fae.. not average but.. most kindred die in the first 5 years so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-02T20:38:22-07:00","id":1393734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rucun</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393615-elders-in-changeling-the-dreaming?p=1393695#post1393695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I Belive a changeling with multiple 5 dot arts and complete mastery over realms will be on equal footing with a mathuselah if you also consider that a changeling of such powers will have powerful chimera companions (like dragons) and unique treasures (like a mirror that allows you to cast arts into a target at the other side of the world)<br /> <br /> <br /> While such changeling might not have arts over 5 dots, he beats any mathuselah in sheer versatility. People often sleep on how powerful having all realms really is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, Level 5 Sovereign should give even a Methuselah pause. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-03T15:07:41-07:00","id":1393859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393615-elders-in-changeling-the-dreaming?p=1393734#post1393734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, Level 5 Sovereign should give even a Methuselah pause. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> ALOT of level 6+ powers are &quot;Normal power but hits everyone in the room&quot; scene alone should give your average kindred pause. Turning into a dragon is protean 8... what level of Protean lets me turn everyone in the damn room into dragons?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-05T21:04:42-07:00","id":1394498,"title":"","content":"Besides Arch Arts what would be a good way to represent More then Human level traits. I allow True Fae/Those not with a mortal host to have these, but for Changelings hmm I think maybe I would allow the Lost Ones, those lost to Bedlam and holed up in a Freehold, to have the option to develop beyond human stats to represent they are becoming less human and more like the creatures of Myth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-06T17:41:13-07:00","id":1394673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1393615-elders-in-changeling-the-dreaming?p=1394498#post1394498\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Besides Arch Arts what would be a good way to represent More then Human level traits. I allow True Fae/Those not with a mortal host to have these, but for Changelings hmm I think maybe I would allow the Lost Ones, those lost to Bedlam and holed up in a Freehold, to have the option to develop beyond human stats to represent they are becoming less human and more like the creatures of Myth.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Take the caps off Unleashing would be my suggestion","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T04:15:50-07:00","id":1396847,"title":"","content":"Personally, I would view Changeling power as less about raw statlines, so much as their ability to draw on a vast web of feudlaism, patronage, Oaths, Contracts, a tricked-out Freehold and a panalopy of Treasures that make a mockery of anything a mere Fetish could do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25625-magicjuggler","name":"MagicJuggler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25625_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"127"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-06-16T05:19:48-07:00","id":1396850,"title":"","content":"Siochain are the \u201celders\u201d among the Kithain. Also Lost Ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]}]}